<rml>
<head>
<title>Z2 drzwi</title>
<!--
Example (TSRE displays): a coach's LED panels by and on its doors.

Shape: PKPIC_B11mnouz-70082.sd, four squares (624 x 168, Surface Glass,
RefreshRate 1, Input Car): two on the body by the doors (MAIN), two on
door leaves (DOOR_B, DOOR_D), which slide with the doors. Input Car: the
coach's own document, its four squares sharing it.

Shows the coach's own number on the right (display.car.number: the
timetable's #tsre.cars, else its consist's UiD) and its class from its tags
(car.tags | has('A'): 1, has('B'): 2), and its train (display.train):
- its category, number and name (#tsre.<field> rows), else its timetable
  name;
- where it comes from and goes to: its own (#tsre.origin, #tsre.destination),
  else its first and last stops' stations;
- by its state: the station it stands at and its departure, the one it
  approaches, its terminus, or its next station.

The bottom line in Polish, then in English, 4 s each, by TSRE's function
cycle on the clock (display.clock, seconds after midnight): data binding
only. z2_drzwi_lua.rml does the same with Lua.
-->
<style>
body, div {
    display: block;
}
span {
    display: inline;
}
body {
    margin: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    background-color: #050302;
    color: #ff8c1a;
    font-family: Noto Sans;
}
#panel {
    position: absolute;
    left: 10px;
    top: 6px;
    right: 10px;
    bottom: 6px;
    white-space: nowrap;
    overflow: hidden;
}
/* Room for the coach's number when it has one. */
#panel.numbered {
    right: 150px;
}
#car {
    position: absolute;
    top: 6px;
    right: 10px;
    bottom: 6px;
    width: 130px;
    border-left: 2px #5a3410;
    text-align: center;
}
#car .number {
    font-size: 84px;
    font-weight: bold;
}
#car .class {
    color: #ffb347;
    font-size: 36px;
}
.train {
    font-size: 52px;
    font-weight: bold;
}
.route {
    font-size: 40px;
}
.state {
    color: #ffb347;
    font-size: 32px;
}
</style>
</head>
<body data-model="display">
<!-- The coach's number and class (task scripting 03). -->
<div id="car" data-if="car.number != ''">
    <div class="number">{{car.number}}</div>
    <div class="class" data-if="car.tags | has('A')">1</div>
    <div class="class" data-if="car.tags | has('B')">2</div>
</div>
<div id="panel" data-class-numbered="car.number != ''">
    <!-- The train's fields where it has them, else its timetable name. -->
    <div class="train" data-if="train.line != '' || train.category != '' || train.number != ''">
        {{train.category}} {{train.number}} {{train.name}}
    </div>
    <div class="train" data-if="train.line == '' &amp;&amp; train.category == '' &amp;&amp; train.number == ''">
        {{train.id}}
    </div>

    <div class="route">{{train.origin}} – {{train.destination}}</div>

    <!-- Polish for 4 s, then English for 4 s. -->
    <div data-if="clock | cycle(4, true, false)">
        <div class="state" data-if="train.state == 'standing'">Stacja: {{train.at}} · odjazd {{train.departs}}</div>
        <div class="state" data-if="train.state == 'approaching'">Dojeżdżamy do: {{train.next}}</div>
        <div class="state" data-if="train.state == 'finished'">Koniec biegu</div>
        <div class="state" data-if="train.state != 'standing' &amp;&amp; train.state != 'approaching' &amp;&amp; train.state != 'finished'">
            Następna stacja: {{train.next}}
        </div>
    </div>
    <div data-if="clock | cycle(4, false, true)">
        <div class="state" data-if="train.state == 'standing'">Station: {{train.at}} · departs {{train.departs}}</div>
        <div class="state" data-if="train.state == 'approaching'">Approaching: {{train.next}}</div>
        <div class="state" data-if="train.state == 'finished'">Terminus</div>
        <div class="state" data-if="train.state != 'standing' &amp;&amp; train.state != 'approaching' &amp;&amp; train.state != 'finished'">
            Next station: {{train.next}}
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</rml>
